-- check/bad: an annotation that says ANY type flows through, and a body
-- that compares two of them. On this branch `==` is the `eq` method
-- (`docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md` §3.1), a rigid variable carries
-- exactly the constraints its `where` clause declares (§6.2 Rule U2), and
-- the message is `missing_where_constraint` at the CALL that needs the
-- method — never at the annotation (§10.4). Not `not_equatable` with the
-- `rigid_variable` reason, which would say the type could not be compared
-- rather than what to write.
pub contains : a, List a -> Bool
contains needle xs = List.any xs (\x -> x == needle)
